Explanation:
The 'mint' function is a common function in ERC20 tokens, which allows users to mint new tokens. The vulnerability lies in the lack of a maximum supply check, which allows the owner to set the total supply to any value. This can lead to loss of funds for the spender, as the total supply can exceed the maximum possible supply. The severity of this vulnerability is high because it can potentially damage the token's value. The profitability of this vulnerability is medium because it can lead to financial loss for the spender.